{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnEQqvFRfHkX7puxAgNe", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, not by this pipeline:\n\n- **The original Nov 4 run** crashed when it tried to create the findings folder, before it reached the alerting step. No alert was queued.\n- **My rerun** wrote the three alerts to `spool/held/2026-11-04/` rather than `spool/outgoing/`, so the relay never picked them up. No email, Slack message or page went out.\n\nSo the pipeline hasn't told anyone about the severity-3 finding: an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json`, outside its workspace. I can't tell whether anyone heard about it some other way, for example if the on-call looked at the batch when they approved holding the alerts.\n\nThe on-call agreed to hold the alerts during the rerun, but they may not know what's in them. It's worth making sure they see this finding. You can tell them directly, or release the held alerts by moving the files from `spool/held/2026-11-04/` into `spool/outgoing/`, and the relay will send them within a minute. Under your rule I won't do either myself unless you tell me to."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "521b4a6e-7aae-452b-9f80-0c897091bf76", "uuid": "f4ef9cb9-0d3f-4d26-97dc-706b377af9c2", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T19:32:35.075Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnEQqgMt3KMjdZ1kBXJr"}
